# ============================================================================
# GATE CSE Intelligence - environment template (v6)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO USE:   cp .env.example .env      then fill in what you have.
# Everything (CLI, app, scripts) loads .env automatically - no exports needed.
# NEVER commit .env. Secrets below are never printed by the app; status
# screens only show whether a key is set.
# ============================================================================

# ---------- DATABASE ---------------------------------------------------------
# Option A (default, zero setup): no GATE_DB_URL at all -> local SQLite file
#     data/gate_cse.sqlite is used. Nothing else to do.
#
# Option B (locked target): PostgreSQL 17 + pgvector via Docker
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=choose-a-strong-local-password
# GATE_DB_URL=postgresql+psycopg://gate_user:${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}@127.0.0.1:5432/gate_cse
# After `docker compose up -d`: alembic upgrade head
#
# Option C: explicit SQLite (same as the default, stated)
# GATE_DB_URL=sqlite:///data/gate_cse.sqlite

# ---------- REVIEWER ---------------------------------------------------------
# Name written to the audit log for every human decision (also editable in the app sidebar).
# GATE_REVIEWER=owner

# ---------- LLM PROVIDERS ----------------------------------------------------
# Add the key(s) you have. `auto` (GATE_LLM_PROVIDER=auto, the CLI default
# path, and the app's auto button) picks the FIRST available provider in
# GATE_LLM_PRIORITY order. All providers use the same classification prompt
# and output contract, so they are interchangeable.
#
# GATE_LLM_PROVIDER=auto            # auto | free | mock | gemini | groq | openrouter | anthropic | openai
# GATE_LLM_PRIORITY=gemini,groq,openrouter,anthropic,openai
#
# --- Free routes (question text still leaves your machine) -------------------
# All external calls require GATE_LLM_ALLOW_EXTERNAL=1 below.
#
# Google AI Studio (Gemini) - key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# A FREE TIER exists, but billing is per billing account: a key on a project
# with billing linked is CHARGED per token. The tool cannot see your plan, so
# gemini calls also need GATE_LLM_FREE_PLAN_CONFIRMED=1 below (your
# attestation) or per-run spend approval. Model is REQUIRED - pick a current
# one from https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models (free-tier model
# availability changes; checked 4 Nov 2026: gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-3.5-flash-lite).
# Run python -m src.cli llm-models gemini to see what YOUR key can use, and pin an explicit
# ID: a -latest alias moves between versions. gemini-2.5-* is deprecated (re-routed 1 Dec 2026).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=
# Optional Gemini knobs (defaults are fine; change only after a pilot says so):
# GEMINI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=8192    # a CAP. Thinking models spend part of it on hidden reasoning; a cut-off answer is
#                                  # reported as finishReason=MAX_TOKENS and is not retried.
# GEMINI_THINKING_LEVEL=           # minimal|low|medium|high - sent ONLY if set; an HTTP 400 means your model does not take it
#
# Pacing (all providers, real calls only): requests per MINUTE the run may make, every attempt counts.
# Default 8, deliberately below typical free-tier limits. Google does not publish free-tier numbers on its docs pages:
# read YOUR limits in AI Studio and set this at or below the model's RPM. 0 = no pacing (tests only).
# GATE_LLM_RPM=8
#
# Groq - key: https://console.groq.com/keys
# Same plan caveat as Gemini: free tier exists, billing is account-dependent,
# needs GATE_LLM_FREE_PLAN_CONFIRMED=1 or spend approval. Default model is a
# current production model; if a call says "model not found", check
# https://console.groq.com/docs/models (llama-3.3-70b-versatile was retired
# Aug 2026).
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
#
# OpenRouter - key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Models ending ':free' are listed at $0 by OpenRouter itself (rate-limited).
# A model NOT ending in ':free' is treated as PAID and needs spend approval.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free
#
# --- Paid (only after explicit spend approval per run) -----------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=                 # required for OpenAI: never assumed
#
# Global model override (wins over every provider-specific model):
# GATE_LLM_MODEL=

# ---------- CONSENT GATES ----------------------------------------------------
# Any external LLM call (question text leaves this machine). 1 = allowed.
GATE_LLM_ALLOW_EXTERNAL=0
# Your attestation that your gemini/groq accounts are on FREE plans. The tool
# cannot verify billing from a key; without this, those two providers need
# per-run spend approval instead. OpenRouter ':free' models don't need it.
GATE_LLM_FREE_PLAN_CONFIRMED=0
# Paid calls are never enabled here: they need --allow-spend (CLI) or the
# per-run "I approve PAID spend" checkbox (app) every single time.

# ---------- FreeLLMAPI: ONE local router key for every chat-LLM call (v12) ----------
# Owner decision 2026-11-05: all chat LLM calls go through the local FreeLLMAPI router
# (http://127.0.0.1:3001, Docker). Add provider keys in ITS dashboard; this project holds only the
# unified 'freellmapi-...' key. Save it with:  python -m src.cli set-key freellmapi   (hidden prompt)
# See docs/23_LLM_ROUTER_AND_DECISION_MODELS.md
# GATE_LLM_PROVIDER=freellmapi
# GATE_LLM_PRIORITY=freellmapi
# GATE_LLM_ROUTER_ONLY=1             # ignore direct provider keys entirely
# FREELLMAPI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3001/v1
# FREELLMAPI_MODEL=auto              # auto | auto:smart | auto:fast | auto:<profile> | exact model id
# FREELLMAPI_API_KEY=

# ---------- Decision models (PAID, separate from FreeLLMAPI, off by default) ----------
# Typed topic choice with calibrated probabilities -> classification_proposals only.
# Real calls need: key + DECISIONS_ENABLED=1 + --yes --allow-spend --max-calls N.
# DECISIONS_ENABLED=0
# OPENAI_DECISIONS_API_KEY=          # python -m src.cli set-key openai-decisions
# OPENAI_DECISIONS_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=                  # python -m src.cli set-key jev
# JEV_MODEL=jev-1.14.0
